{"title":"2013 Mock AIME I Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, each of unit radius, have centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/894f5ddd6708ea9eccd15a525553ebd0fc4d565a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef100258eefc3cb01f88675aaf511c44213fbf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be a circle externally tangent to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> have a common tangent that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  If this tangent is also a common tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, find the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered positive integer triplets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> evenly divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91927ed6d1093e6ce84e3aa8446121218cb17b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> evenly divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4ac9006f8be8d4671f10e68c2ba292528af22af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-a=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> be the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eefa9c7e0a1e3e82de66018f99631a9e5b9e9c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}=x-\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5387384ac2ee9b5617cf02bd2a98be93ea34fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=(7+4\\sqrt{3})^{2^{2013}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"24\" />, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f7086b8f404f1363cd5a12a95cabf3ec81e536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\left(1-\\{x\\}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the number of ways to fill in the following magic square such that:\n</p><p>1. the product of all rows, columns, and diagonals are equal (the sum condition is waived),\n</p><p>2. all entries are <i>nonnegative</i> integers less than or equal to ten, and\n</p><p>3. entries CAN repeat in a column, row, or diagonal.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fdbd63c43e4345cf06b18956239b7aa40ec839.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c35c53b71ea0f1757a360892c1880bcea643aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cap BD=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" />.  Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4d43acfae78520a6ab233719aa54793048fdd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA=6, MB=8, MC=4, MD=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"293\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732732ade118649f003bf202ec3737bdafa9c0c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=2CD$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />.  The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e29a76216d1250df9f2d45380bb908ccf2d1c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p\\sqrt{q}}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime number.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of integer values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can have such that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a0679c9612e94f6b3c566f42ce670f09a1caa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7\\cos x+5\\sin x=2k+1\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" /> has a solution.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th primitive roots of unity with imaginary part greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th primitive roots of unity with imaginary part greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  (A primitive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th root of unity is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th root of unity that is not a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th root of unity for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacf25d4af4a6aa4f5bd06627287b00c491913b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />.)Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b567d569a53db7cabe174e936b2b6d5dacd6b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\sum_{s\\in S}\\sum_{t\\in T}(s+t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"142\" height=\"39\" />.  The absolute value of the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime numbers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd271e80ea9450267d79d49889b0f75aabdd3c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{u}=4\\textbf{i}+3\\textbf{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba589d2a5d4e2703c96e9daf82dcfe8af91a0d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{v}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> be two perpendicular vectors in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> plane. If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16eefaa9b9706d7922adb50cc8c55ae08ce8e3f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{r}_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64a74548c2de93778bf6a16d606bab02dfb7857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1, 2, \\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> in the same plane having projections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d3120fdc109eef89be02d682ed6d7cf986c126c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{u}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"7\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba589d2a5d4e2703c96e9daf82dcfe8af91a0d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{v}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> respectively, then find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e075e37256e83fd0fe0750b0bbbeba797b78802.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\|\\textbf{r}_i\\|^2.\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"47\" /> (Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6019156acbe87272770608b1b898c8edade72538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{i}$\" width=\"5\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1633605f4a353f3f3e0e02acf09d27d42294a84a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"5\" height=\"14\" /> are unit vectors such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164beaf89157930abc6334f50807d251b3f1a6c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{i}=(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/7146322df2696263906ad24cc5392c257e52c987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{j}=(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, and the projection of a vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717da28bae16c5278edc769cf42c1eedd7e1ddcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{a}$\" width=\"9\" height=\"7\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a60477ea66583b3811740d07d8161b0b935d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{b}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> is the length of the vector that is formed by the origin and the foot of the perpendicular of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717da28bae16c5278edc769cf42c1eedd7e1ddcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{a}$\" width=\"9\" height=\"7\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a60477ea66583b3811740d07d8161b0b935d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{b}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a magic circuit, there are six lights in a series, and if one of the lights short circuit, then all lights after it will short circuit as well, without affecting the lights before it. Once a turn, a random light that isn’t already short circuited is short circuited. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the expected number of turns it takes to short circuit all of the lights, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3796ffdb09e156a707f9fe32d25d464dd4b9d1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100E$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> denote the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th triangular number, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfac7082931a03b8b20b1549241eb03217f35580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n=1+2+3+\\cdots+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"15\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be relatively prime positive integers so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa8b65deee59ad25cfb6da6637ab4d1b8878fb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=3}^\\infty \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\left(\\dfrac{3}{T_i}\\right)^k=\\dfrac{m}{n}.\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"50\" />  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789268a0f9be4380d7d127638260206ea244344a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+2x-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/5091308e936050a632af51f4e05eae4c1cd334c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a}{b}+\\dfrac{b}{c}+\\dfrac{c}{a}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/0342c3760525773046249898acfd4b983ec1da1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(X+1)(Y+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line connecting the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/73386bdab820ef20d60d39315582afe275895342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcaee811e84b7f16d962223d7047c61037add076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot BC$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In acute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the orthocenter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the centroid, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f240f06450bc379ecfbf624a12a7b43be1206153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\ge GM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fe8c42e41c03c98a7c213c435a311dea0cca30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM \\ge HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> does not always hold. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337b833c3807f72484c4bccc00ee24bbfd0be814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = 162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ed1469a9f377b72a3ba727f83a96599f866c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e46a5d559ffff94b22f2df24968accfa7438cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> which produces the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fe8c42e41c03c98a7c213c435a311dea0cca30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM \\ge HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560d59a8b28eefaa0b822421f1a78e64d155c1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> squarefree. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f7b62ce7ddf3ad3220094bb7b9122709dfdb84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}P(x) = x^{2013}+4x^{2012}+9x^{2011}+16x^{2010}+\\cdots + 4052169x + 4056196 = \\sum_{j=1}^{2014}j^2x^{2014-j}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"669\" height=\"52\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746aa32454cba266e061c79d5246d030d8333dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots a_{2013}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"11\" /> are its roots, then compute the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8bf28e325e78ce062348156c92033526fa1079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^{997}+a_2^{997}+\\cdots + a_{2013}^{997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" /> is divided by 997.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a39307e79deccf12e78d2549119273d1ad2e9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n | (a^{n+1}-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Compute the remainder when the sum of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I\">2013 Mock AIME I</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Answer Key\">2013 Mock AIME I Answer Key</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055857\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 677/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21783/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20162:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055857 and revision id 223962. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>